4. Belief Compression and Information Constraint

4.1 Variational Information Bottleneck

The belief encoder \phi_{\mathrm{enc}}:\mathcal{O}\times\mathcal{M}\to\mathcal{B} maps observations and memory to beliefs. The memory compressor \phi_{\mathrm{comp}}:\mathcal{B}\times\mathcal{R}\to\mathcal{M} maps beliefs and resources to memory. The information constraint is

\mathcal{I}(s_t;m_t)\le\mathbb{E}\left[\mathrm{KL}(q(s_t\mid m_t)\|p(s_t))\right]\le C_m.

4.2 Constrained Optimisation Formulation

We treat the encoder as a constrained optimisation problem with Lagrangian

\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{enc}}(\theta_{\mathrm{enc}},\nu)=-\mathbb{E}[\log p(o_t\mid s_t)]+\nu\left(\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{KL}(q(s_t\mid m_t)\|p(s_t))]-C_m\right),

where \nu\ge0 is the dual variable for the information budget. The primal-dual dynamics are

\theta_{\mathrm{enc}}\leftarrow\theta_{\mathrm{enc}}-\zeta\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{enc}}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{enc}},\qquad
\nu\leftarrow[\nu+\zeta_\nu(\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{KL}]-C_m)]_+.

4.3 Continuity Through Compression

The composition m=\phi_{\mathrm{comp}}(\phi_{\mathrm{enc}}(o,m_{t-1}),\rho) is Lipschitz with constant L_{\mathrm{comp}}L_{\mathrm{enc}}. This modulus enters the belief-continuity bound of §2.2 and the ergodicity argument of §8.

