9. Safety and Near-Optimality

9.1 Safety Guarantee

Theorem 12 (Resource Constraint Satisfaction). Under the dual update, the expected cumulative cost satisfies

\limsup_{T\to\infty}\frac{1}{T}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathcal{C}(a_t,m_t)\right]\le\rho_0+O\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{T}}\right).

Proof. The dual variable \lambda_t increases whenever the constraint is violated. By Theorem 8, \lambda_t\to\lambda^\star, and complementary slackness \lambda^{\star\top}(\mathbb{E}_\pi[\sum_t\gamma^t\mathcal{C}]-\rho_0)=0 implies the constraint is satisfied in the limit. The O(1/\sqrt{T}) term arises from the stochastic approximation error. \square

9.2 Near-Optimality

Theorem 13 (Near-Optimality). The policy \pi_{\phi^\star} obtained by BUDT-AC satisfies

J(\pi_{\phi^\star})\ge J(\pi^\star)-\frac{2\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}}}{1-\gamma}-O\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{T}}\right),

where \pi^\star is the optimal policy for the constrained problem.

Proof. By the performance difference lemma,

J(\pi^\star)-J(\pi_{\phi^\star})=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{(m,\rho)\sim\mu_{\pi^\star}}\left[A^{\pi_{\phi^\star}}(m,\rho,\pi^\star(m,\rho))\right].

The advantage function is bounded by the approximation error of the value function, which is O(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}}/(1-\gamma)). The stochastic approximation error contributes O(1/\sqrt{T}). \square

9.3 Regret Guarantee

Theorem 14 (Regret Bound). The cumulative regret of BUDT-AC satisfies

\mathbb{E}[R_T]\le\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{d\sqrt{T}}{1-\gamma}\right)+O(\sqrt{T}).

Proof. Combine the frequentist regret bound of Theorem 6 with the contraction modulus \gamma. The (1-\gamma)^{-1} factor arises from the infinite-horizon discounting. \square

