Appendix C: Conformal Calibration Details

C.1 Non-Conformity Scores and Quantile

Given the prior policy \pi_{\mathrm{LLM}}, define

S_t(a)=1-\pi_{\mathrm{LLM}}(a\mid m_t).

Let \mathcal{W}=\{S_1,\dots,S_n\} be the calibration window. The empirical quantile at level 1-\alpha_t is

\hat{q}_t=\inf\left\{q:\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^n\mathbf{1}\{S_j\le q\}\ge1-\alpha_t\right\}.

C.2 Conformal Feasible Set

\mathcal{C}_t=\{a\in\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{valid}}(m_t,\rho_t):S_t(a)\le\hat{q}_t\}.

Lemma C.1 (Non-emptiness). If \mathcal{C}_t=\emptyset, setting

\mathcal{C}_t=\left\{\arg\min_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{valid}}(m_t,\rho_t)}S_t(a)\right\}

preserves non-emptiness and minimises the deviation from the conformal threshold.

C.3 Adaptive Conformal Inference

The ACI update is

\alpha_{t+1}=\alpha_t+\gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}}(\alpha_{\mathrm{conf}}-\mathrm{err}_t),\qquad
\mathrm{err}_t=\mathbf{1}\{a^\star(m_t)\notin\mathcal{C}_t\},

with clipping \alpha_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathrm{clip}(\alpha_{t+1},0,1).

C.4 Coverage Guarantee

Theorem C.1 (ACI Coverage). The ACI update ensures

\left|\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^T\mathrm{err}_t-\alpha_{\mathrm{conf}}\right|\le\frac{\max\{\alpha_1,1-\alpha_1\}+\gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}}}{T\gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}}}+\frac{n_{\mathrm{fallback}}}{T},

where n_{\mathrm{fallback}} is the number of fallback steps.

Proof. The ACI recursion can be rewritten as

\alpha_{t+1}=\alpha_t+\gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}}(\alpha_{\mathrm{conf}}-\mathrm{err}_t).

Telescoping and using 0\le\alpha_{t+1}\le1,

\gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}}\sum_{t=1}^T(\alpha_{\mathrm{conf}}-\mathrm{err}_t)=\alpha_{T+1}-\alpha_1.

Taking absolute values and bounding |\alpha_{T+1}-\alpha_1|\le\max\{\alpha_1,1-\alpha_1\} yields the first term. Fallback steps contribute an additive correction because the conformal threshold is not applied at those steps. \square

C.5 Delayed Revelation

When a^\star(m_t) is revealed with delay d, the ACI recursion becomes

\alpha_{t+1}=\alpha_t+\gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}}(\alpha_{\mathrm{conf}}-\mathrm{err}_{t-d}).

The coverage bound acquires an additional additive term d/T, which is sharp.

