Appendix D: Bayesian Regret Details

D.1 Information Ratio

Definition D.1. The information ratio is

\Gamma_t=\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Delta_t]^2}{\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{I}_t]},

where \Delta_t is the instantaneous regret and \mathcal{I}_t is the information gain.

Lemma D.1 (Bounded Information Ratio). For the conformal-restricted Thompson sampling policy,

\Gamma_t\le2K\sigma^2.

Proof. The information gain is bounded by the entropy reduction in the posterior. For a K-armed bandit with Gaussian noise variance \sigma^2, the standard bound is \Gamma_t\le2K\sigma^2 (Russo–Van Roy). Restricting to \mathcal{C}_t can only decrease both the regret and the information gain, so the ratio remains bounded. \square

D.2 Regret Bound

Theorem D.1 (Bayesian Regret). Under Assumptions 2–6,

\mathbb{E}[R_T]\le\sqrt{2K\sigma^2\,H_{\pi_{\mathrm{LLM}}}(A^\star)\,T}+\alpha T+O(\sqrt{T}).

Proof. Decompose

R_T=\underbrace{\sum_{t:a_t\in\mathcal{C}_t}\Delta_t}_{R_T^{\mathrm{in}}}+\underbrace{\sum_{t:a_t\notin\mathcal{C}_t}\Delta_t}_{R_T^{\mathrm{out}}}.

For the in-set rounds, the standard information-ratio bound gives \mathbb{E}[R_T^{\mathrm{in}}]\le\sqrt{2K\sigma^2\,H(A^\star)\,T}. For the out-of-set rounds, the ACI rate ensures \mathbb{E}[R_T^{\mathrm{out}}]\le\alpha T+O(\sqrt{T}). \square

Corollary D.1 (Prior Utility). The LLM prior improves the bound relative to uniform iff H_{\pi_{\mathrm{LLM}}}(A^\star)<\log K.

Remark D.1 (Misspecification). If the prior is misspecified, the bound holds with H_{\pi_{\mathrm{LLM}}}(A^\star) replaced by the entropy of the prior, which is robust but potentially larger.

