Appendix E: Frequentist Regret via Linear UCB

E.1 Confidence Ellipsoid

Let V_t=\lambda I+\sum_{s=1}^t x_sx_s^\top and

\Theta_t=\left\{\theta\in\mathbb{R}^d:\|\theta-\hat{\theta}_t\|_{V_t}\le\sqrt{\beta_t}\right\},

where \hat{\theta}_t=V_t^{-1}\sum_{s=1}^t x_sy_s and \beta_t is the OFUL radius from Abbasi-Yadkori et al. (2011).

E.2 Regret Bound

Theorem E.1 (Frequentist Regret). The linear UCB policy restricted to \mathcal{C}_t achieves

\mathbb{E}[R_T]\le\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T})+O(\sqrt{T}).

Proof. The OFUL analysis gives \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T}) for the unrestricted policy. Since \mathcal{C}_t\subseteq\mathcal{A}, the restricted regret is bounded by the unrestricted regret plus the out-of-set conformal overhead O(\sqrt{T}). \square

Remark E.1. This improves the \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d^{3/2}\sqrt{T}) rate of linear Thompson sampling to the minimax-optimal \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T}).

