Appendix G: Dual Convergence with Corrected Sign

G.1 Dual Problem

The Lagrangian is

\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)=J(\pi)-\lambda^\top\left(\mathbb{E}_\pi\left[\sum_t\gamma^t\mathcal{C}(a_t,m_t)\right]-\rho_0\right).

The dual problem is

\min_{\lambda\ge0}\max_{\phi\in\Phi}\mathcal{L}(\phi,\lambda).

G.2 Zero Duality Gap

Theorem G.1 (Zero Duality Gap). Under Assumptions 2–4 and the Slater condition (Assumption 4), the constrained MDP has zero duality gap:

\min_{\lambda\ge0}\max_{\phi\in\Phi}\mathcal{L}(\phi,\lambda)=\max_{\phi\in\Phi}\min_{\lambda\ge0}\mathcal{L}(\phi,\lambda).

Proof. The occupancy-measure representation of the constrained MDP is convex for stochastic policies (Paternain et al., 2019). Under the Slater condition, strong duality holds, and the saddle point exists:

\mathcal{L}(\phi,\lambda^\star)\le\mathcal{L}(\phi^\star,\lambda^\star)\le\mathcal{L}(\phi^\star,\lambda)\quad\forall(\phi,\lambda)\in\Phi\times\Lambda.

The dual variable is bounded in \Lambda=[0,\lambda_{\max}] with \lambda_{\max}=\mathbf{1}/((1-\gamma)\xi), where \xi is the feasibility margin. \square

G.3 Dual Update

The corrected projected dual descent is

\lambda_{t+1}=\left[\lambda_t+\eta_t\left(\mathbb{E}_\pi\left[\sum_{s=t}^\infty\gamma^{s-t}\mathcal{C}(a_s,m_s)\right]-\rho_0\right)\right]_+.

Theorem G.2 (Dual Convergence). Under Assumptions 5–9, the dual update converges to \lambda^\star.

Proof. The dual function d(\lambda)=\max_{\phi\in\Phi}\mathcal{L}(\phi,\lambda) is convex in \lambda. The projected stochastic gradient descent on d(\lambda) converges to \lambda^\star under the Robbins–Monro conditions. The sign of the update ensures that \lambda increases when the constraint is violated. \square

Remark G.1. If the sign were reversed (as in the original formulation), the dual variable would decrease when the constraint is violated, violating the complementary slackness condition and preventing convergence to \lambda^\star.

